The maintainer wants Docker-shipped MCP servers to be as easy to mount as npx ones: name the image, the hub pulls, starts, wires the port, talks to it and stops it when idle -- no hand-written `docker run`, no separately managed container. Optional: a compose project directory ("Ziel-Directory").

Design (agent-written, maintainer said "design it, I will tune later"): docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-03-docker-upstreams-design.md

## Done
- New entry kinds `docker` (stdio container; with `port` an HTTP container) and `compose` (directory + `url`), plus `volumes`, `docker_args`, `port`, `path`; `hub.docker_command`, `hub.docker_network`.
- Lazy start / idle stop / always_on / crash-loop / refresh / reload behave as for stdio; manifest hash never over env; no secret in any argv; cleanup touches only containers with this hub's owner label.
- Hub Docker image ships the compose plugin; docker-compose.yml + README document socket, network and host-path gotchas.
- Tests against a fake docker CLI (no real daemon, no network); `prove -lr t/` green.

