Drift for this board: (1) Upstream::Stdio::_on_close does a blocking waitpid($pid,0); under EV libev usually reaps first, so the exit reason/code is often lost, and a child that closes stdout but lingers blocks the loop — the run_p pattern fixes it. (2) Upstream::Http::_close_sse sets {stopping} and nothing clears it, so after a reconnect a dropped SSE stream never moves ready→stopped. (3) Idle-timer code is duplicated in Upstream::Stdio and Upstream::Docker; could move to the base class (touches Stdio, so left out).

